# Walkthrough: Unified Tri-Model Execution for Any Corridor

We have created the end-to-end unified orchestrator [`run_any_corridor.py`](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/run_any_corridor.py) and backend pipeline [`backend/app/engine/corridor_pipeline.py`](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/app/engine/corridor_pipeline.py). 

You can now input **ANY two locations** (landmarks, addresses, or GPS coordinates) and execute **all 3 core research models** together in a single automated command:
1. **Model 1 (Subterranean Storm Drainage)**: CPHEEO pipe conveyance, inlet absorption & manhole surcharges.
2. **Model 2 (2D Hydrodynamic Flood Simulation)**: 2D Saint-Venant overland runoff, depression ponding & rainfall nowcasting.
3. **Model 3 (Flood-Resilient Routing)**: A* pathfinding with vehicle clearance constraints, avoiding submerged streets.

---

## 💻 How to Run It

### Interactive Mode:
Simply run without arguments and follow the prompts:
```bash
.venv\Scripts\python run_any_corridor.py
```

### Direct CLI Mode (Kolkata Kestopur $\rightarrow$ Ruby Corridor, 12 km):
```bash
.venv\Scripts\python run_any_corridor.py --src "Kestopur" --dst "Ruby Hospital" --scenario cloudburst --vehicle car --horizon 60
```

### Direct CLI Mode (Mumbai BKC $\rightarrow$ Kurla Basin, 2x2 km):
```bash
.venv\Scripts\python run_any_corridor.py --src "BKC" --dst "Kurla Station" --scenario heavy --vehicle car --horizon 30
```

### Custom GPS Coordinates Mode:
```bash
.venv\Scripts\python run_any_corridor.py --src "22.5930, 88.4230" --dst "22.5135, 88.4030" --scenario heavy --vehicle suv
```

